      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town grew around Fort Lopeño, a 1821 home‑fort‑chapel built by Benito Ramírez that later hosted federal troops in 1856.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lope%C3%B1o%2C_Texas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the early 1900s Serafín Benavides opened the only general store, the community’s first supply point.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lope%C3%B1o%2C_Texas",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A post office opened in 1920, marking Lopeño’s first federal presence.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lope%C3%B1o%2C_Texas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Oil and gas drilling began in 1934, bringing the first industrial activity to the area.",
